; ============================================================================
; bench_cpp\strbuild.logo -- the string-concatenation workload, for the
; SectorLogo C++ port. See fib.logo for why these four files exist; the result
; is 2001 bytes ("x" plus 2000 "y"s), checked in bench_sectorlogo.logo's gate
; block.
;
; This is the workload where the two ports are most worth separating, because
; the answer is a STRING on a cons-free buffer and the cost is dominated by the
; copy that each `_` does. `_` is the infix concat operator, and the parentheses
; around the two operands are what make the infix spelling legal.
; ============================================================================

Define "strbuild" [:steps] [                        ; strbuild n -- "x" followed by n copies of "y"
  Local "grown"                                     ; the string under construction
  Make "grown" "x"
  Repeat :steps [
    Make "grown" ( :grown _ "y" )                    ; `_` is infix concat -- its copy dominates the cost
  ]
  Output :grown
]

Strbuild 2000                                       ; the benchmark sample: expected 2001 bytes
